<title>NETHERLANDS: RESEARCH - ING Barings cuts KLM estimates.</title>
<headline>RESEARCH - ING Barings cuts KLM estimates.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1996-11-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Summary of Q2 results note.</p>
<p>    Company----------Sector--------Price---Broker----------------</p>
<p>    KLM Royal Dutch  Airlines	41.50   ING Barings</p>
<p>COMMENT: Sell (unchanged). Q2 results show alarming cost development of 15 percent. Compared to capacity increase of 7 percent this was excessive. Full year net forecast further downgraded, due to general rise in costs but more particularly higher fuel costs which to weigh as unforeseen 150 million guilders on 1996/97 net profit. Restructuring will require provisions in 1996/97 H2. Downgrade to 1997/98 EPS forecast should signal bottom if restructuring is successful.</p>
<p>    Estimates (Dfl):   EPS	pvs	P/E     Dividend</p>
<p>    1995 (actual)	5.86		  8.7     2.00</p>
<p>    1996		   4.20     5.20     9.9     N/A</p>
<p>    1997		   3.21     4.10     13.0    N/A</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom, +31 20 504 5000 (Fax +31 20 504 5040)</p>
